-- 20. WADUK GAJAH MUNGKUR (Wonogiri)
(
    'gajahmungkur',
    'Waduk Gajah Mungkur', 'Waduk Gajah Mungkur',
    'The Great Reservoir of Wonogiri', 'The Great Reservoir of Wonogiri',
    'nature', 'Wonogiri, Central Java', 'Near Yogyakarta',
    '["https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506905925346-21bda4d32df4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1470071459604-3b5ec3a7fe05?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80","https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1501785888041-af3ef285b470?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80"]'::jsonb,
    4.5, 2400,
    'Waduk Gajah Mungkur (Gajah Mungkur Reservoir) is a massive reservoir spanning over 8,800 hectares in Wonogiri. Built in the 1970s, it serves as a vital irrigation source and hydropower facility while offering stunning water landscapes with scattered islands. Visitors enjoy boat tours, water sports, camping, and bird watching against a backdrop of rolling hills.',
    'Waduk Gajah Mungkur (Gajah Mungkur Reservoir) is a massive reservoir spanning over 8,800 hectares in Wonogiri. Built in the 1970s, it serves as a vital irrigation source and hydropower facility while offering stunning water landscapes with scattered islands. Visitors enjoy boat tours, water sports, camping, and bird watching against a backdrop of rolling hills.',
    'The reservoir was constructed between 1974 and 1981 as part of the Bengawan Solo river management project. The construction submerged several villages, and over 1,000 families were relocated. The name ''Gajah Mungkur'' comes from a nearby hill that resembles a crouching elephant. Today, the reservoir has become a vital economic and tourism hub for Wonogiri.',
    'The reservoir was constructed between 1974 and 1981 as part of the Bengawan Solo river management project. The construction submerged several villages, and over 1,000 families were relocated. The name ''Gajah Mungkur'' comes from a nearby hill that resembles a crouching elephant. Today, the reservoir has become a vital economic and tourism hub for Wonogiri.',
    'IDR 10,000 / person / IDR 50,000 – 200,000 for boat tours',
    '06:00 AM – 06:00 PM Daily',
    '["Reservoir Viewpoint","Boat Tours (Motor & Paddle)","Water Sports","Camping Grounds","Bird Watching Tower","Lakeside Restaurants","Parking Area","Restrooms"]'::jsonb,
    '["Reservoir Viewpoint","Boat Tours (Motor & Paddle)","Water Sports","Camping Grounds","Bird Watching Tower","Lakeside Restaurants","Parking Area","Restrooms"]'::jsonb,
